WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:02.869
India's economy grew 9.2

2
00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.943
percent in 2023-24.

3
00:00:05.243 --> 00:00:07.718
Now the official figure says 7.2.

4
00:00:08.218 --> 00:00:09.839
The economy didn't change.

5
00:00:10.139 --> 00:00:11.633
The measuring tape did.

6
00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:14.482
On 27 February 2026, the

7
00:00:14.482 --> 00:00:18.298
statistics office moved GDP's base year

8
00:00:18.418 --> 00:00:21.618
from 2011-12 to 2022-23.

9
00:00:22.068 --> 00:00:23.683
Rebasing updates the prices

10
00:00:23.683 --> 00:00:25.716
and weights used to add up output,

11
00:00:25.836 --> 00:00:27.793
and brings in new data, like

12
00:00:27.793 --> 00:00:29.889
GST records and fresh surveys.

13
00:00:30.339 --> 00:00:31.650
So some years went down,

14
00:00:31.650 --> 00:00:32.579
and some went up:

15
00:00:32.699 --> 00:00:36.312
2024-25 rose from 6.5 to

16
00:00:36.312 --> 00:00:38.118
7.1 percent.

17
00:00:38.568 --> 00:00:40.488
Same farms, same factories.

18
00:00:40.638 --> 00:00:41.705
A new ruler.

19
00:00:42.205 --> 00:00:43.015
Your turn!

20
00:00:43.135 --> 00:00:45.333
What does rebasing GDP change?
